<th id="S4.T3.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;" colspan="3"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    Network    </span></th></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    Policy    </span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    </span><math id="S4.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.2.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    </span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    </span><math id="S4.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.2.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    </span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.5.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    </span><math id="S4.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.2.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    </span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T3.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    </span><math id="S4.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    </span></th>
<td id="S4.T3.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    87.92    </span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    87.95    </span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    87.08    </span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    </span><math id="S4.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.5.4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    </span></th>
<td id="S4.T3.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    87.68    </span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    87.71    </span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    63.70    </span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b ltx_border_rr" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    Random    </span></th>
<td id="S4.T3.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    87.79    </span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    88.06    </span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding:0.4pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">    82.50    </span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we ask: is there anything special about the network and policy pairing, or are the networks themselves robust/brittle to other quantization policies as well? To examine this, we focused on the ResNet18 white box model and the highlighted ResNet18 networks then applied all combinations of <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, and random quantization (still maintaining the specified budget <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>). In Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.1 Obtaining Robust and Detrimental Policies ‣ 4 EXPERIMENTS ‣ Assessing the Potential for Catastrophic Failurein Dynamic Post-Training Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we see that the base white box model <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is already fairly robust to each of the quantization policies, but <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is slightly more robust which should be expected. Interestingly, we do see a significant connection between <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of detrimental behavior. When utilizing the robust policy <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, we observe a <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 1\%</annotation></semantics></math> reduction in accuracy, much less than the <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 24.4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>24.4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 24.4\%</annotation></semantics></math> degradation seen with <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is not brittle to all quantization policies. Furthermore, <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> has likely identified some “weak points” in <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and is exploiting those to induce catastrophic failure whereas <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> does not exploit these vulnerabilities.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Network Layer Analysis</h3>

<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="S4.F2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
